- Hearing logistics
  - How long will I have to present my case? What order should evidence/witnesses be presented in?
  - How many copies of exhibits should I bring, and in what format (exhibit binder, pads, electronic)?
  - What will the judge expect on hearing day (dress, arrival time, check-in procedure)?
- Post-judgment and enforcement
  - If we win, how do we enforce the judgment (writs, garnishment, levy)? If we lose, what are appeal options or other remedies?
- Specific questions about interactions
  - How should I answer questions from opposing counsel or the judge if they ask something we don’t have an immediate answer for?
  - Are there phrases or admissions I should avoid saying in court?

B. Documents and evidence checklist (bring originals + organized copies)
- Lease / rental agreement (signed copy)
- Notices served (3/30/60-day, pay/quit, termination): copies with proof of service (signed receipt, certified mail, process server declaration)
- Rent ledger & payment receipts (bank records, money orders, Venmo, checks) showing amounts/dates
