Courtroom conduct and testimony tips
- Speak only when asked, answer verbally and directly, pause to think, avoid shouting or arguing.
- Use dates and concrete numbers where possible. If you don’t know, say “I don’t know” rather than guessing.
- Bring multiple sets of exhibits and your timeline. Give copies to the judge and opposing counsel early.
- Dress neatly and arrive early. Bring a notebook and pen.

