- What is the next court date and what will happen at that hearing (pretrial, settlement conference, trial)?
- Are there any filing deadlines or forms I must submit before the hearing (exhibit lists, witness lists, pretrial statement)?
- Will mediation be required/available? Should we propose mediation?
- If this is small claims, can you attend court with me or only help me prepare? (California small claims usually restrict lawyers from appearing for parties.)

Evidence & documents
- Which documents are most persuasive in this case and why?
- Are there any documents I still need to obtain or create (receipts, repair estimates, declarations, proof of service)?
- How should I organize exhibits and how many copies do I need for the judge, opposing party, and my own set?
- Do we need signed witness declarations? Which witnesses should appear in person vs provide written declarations?

Questions about testimony & cross-examination
- What questions is opposing counsel likely to ask me? How should I answer them succinctly?
- What questions should I ask the opposing party or their witnesses?
- What objections are appropriate if the other side offers certain evidence (hearsay, relevance)? In this venue, how strictly will rules be applied?

Strategy & outcomes
- What are the realistic outcomes and possible damages? What are the costs vs benefits of proceeding?
- What evidence or arguments are the strongest for our case and what are our weak spots?
- If settlement is offered, what minimum terms should I accept or reject?

Logistics & courtroom procedure
- What time should I arrive, where to check in, and what to bring (ID, copies, binder)?
- How long will I be allowed to speak/testify? Are there local time limits or judge preferences I should know about?
- How will exhibits be introduced? Any particular labeling format the court prefers?

Follow-up & appeals
- If we win/lose, what are next steps (judgment collection, motion to vacate, appeal timeline)?
- How do we enforce any judgment (garnishment, writ of possession, etc.) in San Diego County?

Specific to landlord-tenant / eviction evidence checklist
