- “Have you tried to resolve this outside of court?” (Show communications or offer summary.)
- “Is there anything the court should know about attempts to mitigate?” (Explain steps taken.)

Evidence and admissibility notes
- Keep original documents when possible; have copies dated and labeled.
- If a witness won’t attend, ask Maria whether a written declaration is acceptable in your court.
- In small claims the court may be more flexible about hearsay and formal rules; however, evidentiary objections can still matter—ask Maria how strict your judge typically is.

