B. Questions to ask your attorney (what you should ask Maria)
- Case status and timeline
  - What are the next steps now that discovery is closed? When should we expect a hearing date?
  - How long will the hearing likely be and what should I expect on the hearing day?
- Burden of proof and legal standard
  - What exactly is our burden of proof at the hearing? What must I prove (or what must the other side prove)?
  - What specific law or code sections will the judge apply?
- Evidence and documents
  - Which documents are most important to present? Do you recommend any further documents or records I should compile?
  - How should documents be organized and authenticated (copies for the judge, exhibits for opposing counsel)?
- Witnesses and testimony
  - Do we need witnesses? If so, who should testify and what will they be asked?
  - Should we subpoena anyone (witnesses, records from third parties, police reports, maintenance logs)?
- Procedural issues
